<!--
    GRTubeYou: thumbs down, resting state.

    The real Material `thumb_down_off_alt` outline - a dedicated down-thumb, not the up-thumb
    rotated, flipped or scaled. The previous version here was a hand-mixed path: the filled
    down-thumb outline with the *outlined* variant's inner cut appended, which rendered as a
    broken shape that read as a transformed up-thumb. The whole point of a thumb pair is that
    they are two different silhouettes from one set.

    Same 24x24 grid, same view box and same stroke width as comment_thumb_up, so the two line
    up when they sit next to each other in the action row. Hollow at rest, filled from
    comment_thumb_down_active when the comment is downvoted.
-->
